        "execSummary":  "Google\u0027s demonstration that multi-agent orchestration can resolve open problems in formal mathematics and build hardware simulators from scratch marks a significant benchmark in what autonomous AI systems can accomplish on long-horizon technical tasks. For enterprise leaders in R\u0026D, engineering, and software development, this signals that multi-agent frameworks are moving from experimental to capable on problems that previously required months of expert human effort. The practical implication is that organizations with large backlogs of complex technical work — codebase modernization, systems design, scientific research — should begin scoping pilot deployments of orchestrated multi-agent systems. Google\u0027s investment in Antigravity as a production platform, not just a research project, suggests this capability will be commercially accessible in the near term.",
