        "summary":  "Google released three new Gemini audio models via the Gemini API and AI Studio: Gemini 3.8 Live for real-time voice agents with reasoning and function-calling capabilities, Gemini 3.8 Live Extended Thinking for complex multi-step reasoning during live conversations, and Gemini 3.5 Transcribe with a 2.6% Word Error Rate supporting 85-plus languages. Pricing starts at $0.005 per minute for audio input, and the models are integrated with developer platforms including Pipecat, LiveKit, LangChain, and Vercel. Gemini 3.8 Live Extended Thinking ranks first on Artificial Analysis\u0027 Speech-to-Speech leaderboard.",
        "execSummary":  "Google\u0027s Gemini 3.8 Live stack delivers enterprise-grade voice AI capabilities — real-time reasoning, function calling, and 97-language support — at commodity pricing that will accelerate replacement of traditional IVR and first-tier human support with AI voice agents. For customer experience and contact center leaders, the combination of Extended Thinking (complex reasoning during live calls) and Transcribe (high-accuracy multilingual STT) removes two longstanding technical blockers to full voice agent deployment. The broad partner ecosystem (LangChain, Vercel, LiveKit) means these capabilities can be integrated into existing contact center platforms without rebuilding infrastructure. Organizations that have deferred voice AI due to accuracy and reasoning limitations should reassess their timelines against these benchmarks.",
