        "execSummary":  "Anthropic\u0027s policy update effective November 12 tightens and clarifies the guardrails governing Claude deployments, with direct implications for enterprise legal and compliance teams. The new surveillance restrictions — prohibiting tracking without consent and limiting law enforcement decision-making assistance — require enterprises in HR, security monitoring, and public sector AI use cases to review deployment configurations before the effective date. The addition of governance rules for autonomous agents connected to physical hardware is a forward-looking signal that Anthropic anticipates rapid growth in physical AI integrations. Compliance officers should treat this update as a changelog requiring a policy gap analysis against current Claude deployments.",
