        "theme":  "Agents",
        "summary":  "Postman implemented Agent Mode using Amazon Bedrock to power AI-driven interactions for its 40 million developer users, discovering that context management and dynamic tool scoping were more critical challenges than raw model capability. The architecture uses cross-region inference for traffic burst handling, geographic data residency controls for enterprise customers, and prompt caching with tiered TTLs to manage costs. The team limited active tools to approximately 15 per task rather than exposing all 170+ available tools, using schema-aware reads and treating the context window as a scarce resource.",
        "execSummary":  "Postman\u0027s Agent Mode deployment at 40 million users reveals a critical architectural insight: in production agentic systems, tool proliferation and context window mismanagement are more likely to cause failures than model quality gaps. For enterprise architects building agent platforms, the \u0027dynamic tool scoping to ~15 active tools\u0027 pattern offers a practical heuristic for reducing hallucination and error rates at scale. The cross-region inference and geographic data residency features address a common enterprise blocker — regulatory compliance — directly at the infrastructure layer. This case study is a strong reference architecture for enterprises deploying developer-facing AI agents on Bedrock.",
