        "title":  "Beyond hours saved: Building the business case for agentic automation",
        "source":  "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "url":  "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/beyond-hours-saved-building-the-business-case-for-agentic-automation/",
        "date":  "2026-10-07",
        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "The article challenges the traditional \u0027hours saved times labor cost\u0027 ROI model for agentic AI automation, arguing it systematically undervalues these systems. The authors introduce an Agentic Value Model measuring four dimensions — time savings, exception handling, decision quality, and change resilience — and demonstrate using real-world examples from Kitsa and dLocal that freed capacity only creates P\u0026L value when redeployed or translated into actual cost reductions. A prioritization matrix based on task complexity and decision risk guides which workflows to automate first.",
        "execSummary":  "This article provides enterprise leaders with a more rigorous financial framework for justifying agentic AI investments beyond simplistic labor-hour math. The four-dimension Agentic Value Model — covering time savings, exception handling, decision quality, and change resilience — gives CFOs and COOs a structured vocabulary for evaluating automation portfolios. The critical point that freed capacity must be explicitly redeployed to hit the P\u0026L is a common pitfall in enterprise automation ROI that this framework directly addresses. Leaders building board-level business cases for agentic automation should use this model to set realistic break-even targets and governance checkpoints.",
