        "summary":  "AWS\u0027s September 2026 recap covers major releases across Amazon Bedrock, AgentCore, and Strands platforms, including Bedrock Managed Agents now supporting OpenAI models with enterprise security features, an improved AgentCore runtime with faster cold starts and pay-as-you-go pricing, and new Strands tools including the Harness framework and Decider 2B decision model. General availability was announced for new language models from OpenAI, Anthropic, Moonshot AI, and xAI on Bedrock. Native data connectors for knowledge bases now cover ServiceNow, Salesforce, Zendesk, and Confluence.",
        "execSummary":  "AWS\u0027s September release velocity signals that Amazon Bedrock is maturing into a full enterprise AI operating platform — not just a model hosting layer — with native integrations to the core enterprise software stack (ServiceNow, Salesforce, Zendesk, Confluence). The addition of OpenAI models to Bedrock Managed Agents is particularly strategic: it lets enterprises standardize on AWS\u0027s security and governance infrastructure regardless of which foundation model they choose. The Decider 2B model and Harness framework for Strands suggest AWS is building opinionated tooling for agent orchestration, reducing the need for bespoke solutions. Platform architects should reassess their multi-cloud AI strategy in light of Bedrock\u0027s rapid expansion into orchestration and data connectivity.",
