        "source":  "NVIDIA AI Blog",
        "url":  "https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/telecom-operators-open-models/",
        "date":  "2026-10-06",
        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "Telecom operators are increasingly adopting open AI models over proprietary solutions, with 89% of respondents in NVIDIA\u0027s State of AI in Telecommunications report calling open source models strategically important. The article identifies five benefits: lower costs, telecom-specific customization, enhanced governance, flexible cloud-to-edge deployment, and locally-adapted enterprise services. Industry examples include SoftBank Corp. building telecom-specific models, AT\u0026T implementing workload-appropriate model selection, and Indosat Ooredoo Hutchison creating Indonesian-language Sahabat-AI models.",
        "execSummary":  "The 89% open model preference among telecom operators reflects a broader enterprise trend: regulated industries with specific domain requirements are choosing customizable open models over black-box proprietary systems for governance and cost reasons. For enterprise AI strategists outside telecom, this signals that open model infrastructure is maturing to the point where it can compete with frontier proprietary models on specialized tasks — a decision point for any industry with domain-specific AI needs. NVIDIA\u0027s positioning of Nemotron and NeMo libraries as the fine-tuning stack for open models makes this as much a hardware and platform play as a model story. Enterprises evaluating build-vs-buy AI decisions should weigh the telecom sector\u0027s open model learnings as a reference for their own vertical specialization strategies.",
